ke I said I I don't think  it I I would never say that Chris  Chibnall that any head writer should be  hired because they were a woman and they  have a female doctor well no as you get  someone who's gonna handle the character  in the story in the show well but  this is one of the reasons why I think  it's important to have diversity in your  writing room in the development process  of more movies of more comic books of  more TV shows because if nothing else  even if you know the head writer or show  creator what have you is stepping  outside their own experience if they can  turn to like literally just terms it was  like oh oh help me you know someone who  has the experience I think that makes a  difference  and it's been helpful you know that he  does seem to have a I would say a  respectable percentage of females on the  writing staff and also hired to direct  the episodes now again does that  automatically mean it will be better  well no Jessica Jones season 2 kind of  made a big song and dance about how  every episode was directed by a woman  that didn't make that season any better  it was a nice thought but that won't  automatically save it any more than  having a female character her handle by  man will automatically ruin it  I just think that it's it's a place  where diversity within the development  process the creative process benefits  everybody because you end up with a  situation where it's much easier to  include greater diversity because you  can turn to someone with the experience  so that it can be integrated naturally  and flow the way a good character or a  good moment should so there we go  how many pervs are gonna call me an sjw  because I ended up unexpectedly making  this a call for diversity I honestly  hadn't planned to go there but that's  where my head went so we'll see but if  you can if you've got any thoughts on  any of this even if you disagree with me  go ahead leave something in the comics  keep it respectful even if you do  disagree